  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Review Desk",
    "overview": "ApplyMate's two surfaces, the Chrome side panel and the localhost dashboard, are one quiet tool UI in the Linear/Raycast family. The panel is a review desk, not a chatbot. Evidence sits on top, conversation sits below, and every change arrives as a card the user approves. The dashboard's application page is the record of one run: what the job asked for, what was sent, and how it got there. Both surfaces share one token set (`lib/ui/tailwind-preset.cjs`, mirrored from the approved `docs/superpowers/mockups/review-chat/tokens.css`).\n\nDensity is calm. Body text is 13.5px system sans on a 4px grid, separated by hairline borders and tonal steps rather than heavy chrome. Color is held back: neutrals carry the structure, a single cobalt accent marks action and \"worked in\", and green and red appear only in word diffs and outcomes. The user rejected two failure modes. One is the support-widget bubble stream. The other is the IDE diff wall: too dense, monospace, raw LaTeX. Diffs render as proportional prose with bold kept.\n\nLight and dark both follow the OS through `prefers-color-scheme`, and `data-theme=\"light|dark\"` on the root pins one. Tokens are CSS custom properties, so components never use `dark:` variants.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "System UI sans at 13.5px, with tabular numerals on the body. No monospace anywhere, including `<kbd>`.",
      "One cobalt accent. Everything else is neutral, plus status and diff hues.",
      "Hairline 1px borders and tonal surfaces (`surface` / `surface-2`). Almost no shadow.",
      "Three radii: chip 4, control 6, card 10, plus fully rounded pills.",
      "Every change is a card with explicit Apply / Dismiss / Undo. Nothing changes silently."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Cobalt Rule",
        "body": "The accent marks only primary actions, the current version, and worked-in keywords. When the accent appears on decoration or as a second emphasis, the hierarchy collapses.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green-Means-Outcome Rule",
        "body": "Green and red appear only in word diffs and in outcomes (applied, refused, error, bridge state). They never act as decoration or category color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Mono Rule",
        "body": "No monospace in the UI. Word diffs are proportional prose, `<kbd>` keys use the sans face, and LaTeX or raw part IDs never reach the screen.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Rule",
        "body": "Every label, heading and button is in sentence case at normal tracking. The system has no uppercase tracked labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Evidence-First Rule",
        "body": "On both surfaces, the evidence (what the job asked for and what was done) comes before conversation or history. The coverage strip always sits directly under the title.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-Desk Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces rest flat. Only the thing waiting on the user's decision, the proposal card, gets lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Nesting Rule",
        "body": "No cards inside cards. Dashboard sections are single hairline boxes with internal row dividers.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every color, size, radius and shadow from the shared preset (`lib/ui/tailwind-preset.cjs`) through its custom properties, so light and dark stay in lockstep.",
      "**Do** keep the accent to primary actions, the current version, and worked-in keywords (The One Cobalt Rule).",
      "**Do** render every resume, letter or answer change as a proposal card with explicit Apply, and keep Undo reachable after applying.",
      "**Do** show diffs as proportional prose with `<ins>`/`<del>` tints and bold preserved.",
      "**Do** use Small (12.75px) for controls and meta, and Body (13.5px) for reading.",
      "**Do** give every interactive element the global `:focus-visible` ring, and honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (all animation and transitions off)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use monospace, LaTeX, or raw part IDs (`r1.b2`) anywhere in the UI.",
      "**Don't** build chat as a bubble stream with avatars. Claude's turns are plain text under a label.",
      "**Don't** nest cards in cards, or lay out the dashboard as stat tiles.",
      "**Don't** use green or red outside diffs and outcomes, or introduce a second accent hue.",
      "**Don't** use stock Tailwind palette classes (`gray-*`, `blue-*`) or `font-bold` headings. Those belong to pre-restyle dashboard pages and are not part of this system.",
      "**Don't** add uppercase tracked labels or eyebrow text above headings."
    ]
  }
}